test: A city of mounds, 15,000 people, 900 years ago, near St Louis. What does it show? | North America had towns long before Europeans came | Europeans built it long ago and then left it empty | Nobody lived in America then | It was a Viking camp
test: In a strategy game, America at the start is shown as empty land. What is wrong? | Many nations lived there already | Nothing, it really was empty | Only animals lived there | Only the Vikings lived there
test: How did the Ancestral Puebloans farm in the desert? | By carefully collecting water | By using huge rivers everywhere | By not farming at all | By buying food from Spain
exam: Identify the period by which humans are known to have reached the Americas. | At least fifteen thousand years ago | Approximately five hundred years ago | Approximately one thousand years ago | Approximately three million years ago
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the indigenous peoples of North America prior to European arrival? | Numerous distinct nations with hundreds of languages | A single nation with one language | An uninhabited continent | A province of the Spanish crown
exam: Ascertain the principal cause of the great mortality among indigenous peoples following contact with Europeans. | Diseases such as smallpox, against which they had no resistance | Volcanic eruptions | A renewed ice age | The failure of the bison herds alone, which left every nation starving
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the Trail of Tears in the 1830s. | The Cherokee were forcibly removed far westward and thousands perished | The Cherokee voluntarily emigrated to Europe | It was a trading route of the Inuit | It was a festival of the Haudenosaunee
